# ==============================================================================
# .netrc Template for Geospatial Data Sources
# ==============================================================================
# The .netrc file (or _netrc on Windows) is used by curl, python libraries, and
# command-line downloaders to authenticate automatically when fetching data.
#
# INSTRUCTIONS FOR SETUP:
# 1. Copy this template file to your user profile directory:
#    - On Windows: C:\Users\<YourUsername>\_netrc   (Note the leading underscore!)
#    - On Mac/Linux: ~/.netrc                      (Note the leading dot!)
# 2. Open that copied file and replace the placeholder credentials below.
# 3. Secure the file permissions:
#    - On Mac/Linux: run `chmod 600 ~/.netrc` to ensure only you can read it.
#    - On Windows: Secure it via file properties to only allow access to your user.
# 4. Crucial: NEVER commit your actual .netrc or _netrc files to Git. The project
#    .gitignore is configured to block them.
# ==============================================================================

# --- NASA Earthdata Login (required by earthaccess, SRTM, MODIS, ASTER downloads) ---
# Sign up at: https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov/
machine urs.earthdata.nasa.gov
  login YOUR_EARTHDATA_USERNAME
  password YOUR_EARTHDATA_PASSWORD

# --- Copernicus Data Space Ecosystem (CDSE) ---
# Sign up at: https://dataspace.copernicus.eu/
# Required for downloading Sentinel-1 (radar), Sentinel-2 (multispectral) imagery
machine dataspace.copernicus.eu
  login YOUR_COPERNICUS_USERNAME
  password YOUR_COPERNICUS_PASSWORD

# --- USGS EarthExplorer ---
# Sign up at: https://earthexplorer.usgs.gov/
# Required for downloading Landsat data and USGS DEMs
machine ers.cr.usgs.gov
  login YOUR_USGS_USERNAME
  password YOUR_USGS_PASSWORD
